It's now around ten years that I ascended (a Knight) for the first time
after trying three years or so.  The only thing I know for sure is that
I got only few wishes (one magic lamp and the castles wand of wishing),
and that my bag of holding with my ascension kit (remove curse, holy
water, all wands, potions of healing, ...) got eaten in an inattentive
moment at Molochs Sanctum(!).  The next ascension (Tourist) followed
exactly two months later.  In that second ascension game I also had not
many wishes (did not use even the castle wand).  All my characters had
always been chosen randomly by the game; until I ascended all character
classes I excluded the already ascended classes by immediately quitting.
So all in all I'd say it must have been more trained skill than luck.
But there are always enough luck factors in NH, and if the RNG does
not like you, you're out of luck... ;-)

